        "a": "No. Apple states that you can create your own HKActivitySummary objects if needed but cannot save them to the store. The objects you read are mutable, but Apple notes that changing their properties has no effect on the values stored in HealthKit. Activity data enters HealthKit through the underlying samples, not through summaries."
